  "orderName": "Diprotodontia",
  "description": "The largest order of marsupials, containing kangaroos, wallabies, possums, wombats, and koalas. Diprotodontia are united by fused lower incisors (hence the name, 'two front teeth') and a syndactylous second and third toe. With over 140 species, they represent the dominant large land mammals of Australasia.",
